       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm sorry, but I won't enter this order as written. A dose of 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled adult dose. It carries a serious risk of harm, and the risk is higher still because the order would run on a continuing schedule. No indication supports it, and I'd be entering it knowingly.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for exceeding the maximum, such as a protocol or a toxicology or specialist recommendation, you can enter it directly in the order system. It would then go through pharmacist verification. If this was a dosing slip, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
